.TH SDL_HINT_APPLE_TV_CONTROLLER_UI_EVENTS 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_APPLE_TV_CONTROLLER_UI_EVENTS \- A variable controlling whether controllers used with the Apple TV generate UI events.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_APPLE_TV_CONTROLLER_UI_EVENTS \(dqSDL_APPLE_TV_CONTROLLER_UI_EVENTS\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
When UI events are generated by controller input, the app will be backgrounded when the Apple TV remote\(aqs menu button is pressed, and when the pause or B buttons on gamepads are pressed\[char46]
.PP
More information about properly making use of controllers for the Apple TV can be found here: https://developer\[char46]apple\[char46]com/tvos/human-interface-guidelines/remote-and-controllers/
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Controller input does not generate UI events\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Controller input generates UI events\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

